{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact5e7a1d2f201ff9863f064860e8e8f4423c601b5c/tree475308c9b2ce393d44757e1649bcbe4f585c07a1, primaryfd0afb95c172162f949807786eb73cd6e39c8063. Hugh's four adopted product decisions can stand; the design needs the bounded authority/recovery contracts below before approval. No implementation is requested by this review.\n\nF1 (Security, high): the Source/audit paragraph asserts that hashing the destination reservation entry makes the choice unpredictable to the author. A deterministic digest adds no entropy, and the note supplies no independently committed randomness or anti-grinding/retry rule. In a quiet room a proposer can control candidate/idempotency inputs or repeatedly cancel/re-reserve until an unaudited attempt appears. That contradicts the claimed deterrent. Specify a replay-verifiable selection with an independent trust/entropy commitment AFTER the member's fixed result/subject and an attempt identity that cancellation/retry cannot resample for free; or limit the first slice to every:1 and leave probabilistic sampling explicitly open. Also require positive bounded every and comparable audited subjects/configurations: a member unit-test result and an unrelated room integration-test result are not evidence that someone lied merely because their booleans differ. Add witnesses for retry/grinding and mismatched audit configuration.\n\nF2 (Architecture/Security, high): published failure/holds is described as one more message and an intent, but an issue record cannot by itself enforce the destination's next admission. Name the native authority that durably records the failed check/subject and affected extent before any later publication it must block, and the verified idempotent failure/recovery exchange. Bind the hold to exact job/check/configuration/rules revision and published subject; for the deploy-check example also name environment/release and observation identity/freshness, or explicitly leave that example dependent on the separate deployment contract. A late success for releaseA must not clear newer failureB, duplicate/reordered notices must not lose a hold, and closing an unrelated intent must not release it. A maintainer's deliberate recorded override/repair permission must be distinguishable from observed health. Timeout/unknown/unavailable evidence is not a pass. Update the published dependency row and witnesses accordingly. This is required to keep landed forge4.8's separation of exact subject, authority, provider outcome and current health; no full UI/API schema is needed here.\n\nF3 (Architecture/Simplification, medium): Reuse needs an unambiguous qualifying-result and recovery rule. The match list includes source, but the disagreement rule drops it; it also does not state stage or which authorized job/result records qualify. Comparing arbitrary earlier claims, a different stage/source, or unauthenticated records can wrongly poison reuse. Conversely immutable old pass+fail remain forever: as written check-disagrees can keep refusing even after the fresh run demanded by the next sentence. State one consistent room/subject/configuration/source/stage/authority eligibility boundary and explicit provenance to the old deciding job; keep existing signer/role/freshness and current-rule checks. Distinguish disabling cache reuse from admitting a new correctly fenced fresh run, while preserving the contradictory history. State a finite explicit-candidate/index lookup rather than an implicit whole-room scan, and make health checks ineligible for content-only reuse. Add a fresh-run-after-conflict witness and an ineligible/different-source prior-result witness. Do not relabel an old job as a new execution.\n\nF4 (Source accuracy, medium): What exists today says only a person can reopen an intent. The cited issue.ts301–329 instead gates reopen-own by issue.close-own and requester identity; membership.ts100 and131/151 include that action for agents. An authorized agent requester can already reopen its own intent. Correct the claim and describe the new automatic published-failure path as the proposed change, not a nonexistent human-only restriction. The checker-role citation membership.ts:13 points to a comment; the relevant role mapping is107, with152 for the initial role list. The dependency table's Nothing open must also expose the unresolved admission/selection/authoritative-state work above (including where the admin-controlled room-service key mark and its rotation are held), not imply publishing new rule values alone supplies those guarantees. Outside evidence basis own-answer/read is an owner-defined observation class, not a self-authenticating provider receipt; keep its exact run-operation owner/trust contract explicitly open as the table intends.\n\nArchitecture conclusion: changes requested for audit/reuse/regression state and dependencies; the source/reuse/stage decomposition and versioned adoption are useful. Security conclusion: changes requested for the claimed sampling guarantee and causally correct hold/result admission. Simplification conclusion: preserve the three plain concepts and existing-room defaults, but replace the unsupported shortcuts with the small explicit state/trust boundaries above; do not expand into an implementation specification. No objection to the four recorded Hugh decisions or the first production adapter being in the slice.\n\nValidation: read the entire bound note and every cited source region at the exact head: rules-scope96–108,extents426–432,membership13 plus actual107/100/131/151–152,outcome66–81,change987–1116,change3:52–75,destination556–605,evidence16–27,issue301–329/551–591; checked merge reports max32 atchange1283. Read landed forge4.8 and independently confirmed that section equals the candidate's reference. All5relative file references resolve, diff--check clean. The branch predates the newly landed forge figures; that is an old base, not a requested deletion, and future local landing must preserve those9paths and all other moved-Main Source. The canonical request asserts its gate passed; no raw private log read or runtime/gate rerun for this prose review, and no independent runtime acceptance claimed. No Source, export, implementation commission, push or deployment approval. Return an exact revised note addressing F1–F4.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fd0afb95c172162f949807786eb73cd6e39c8063","binding":"assigned","head":"5e7a1d2f201ff9863f064860e8e8f4423c601b5c","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:27f224899c5f400d816262f8e8f50027cfe6f6cf\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b7496f05536526e6f153ea60c051c551495b1da0\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:27f224899c5f400d816262f8e8f50027cfe6f6cf","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}